    60	## 2. Enumerator, gates, and what a tuple is
    61	
    62	Gates, in order, are exactly HT §5.3–§5.4 as confirmed by HV §9:
    63	
    64	* `M | N`, `M >= 2`, `kappa = N/M`;
    65	* `2 <= j <= a <= N-2`, so `W = N-a >= 2`;
    66	* ORBIFOLD-CAGE `(C-1)`: `s + s' = M + 2 - j` with `1 <= s,s' <= M`
    67	  (CENTRAL-RANK `r = j-1` is already substituted);
    68	* integer partitions of `M` into `s` (resp. `s'`) parts: local degrees
    69	  `m_i | p`, `l_j | q`, `sum m_i = sum l_j = M`;
    70	* HT §7.3 reconstruction of `p` (symmetrically `q`): if `s = 1` then
    71	  `p = M D` with `D >= 1` and `gcd(D, kappa) = 1` (unbounded); if
    72	  `s >= 2` then `p = lcm(m_i) >= 2`, cone orders `D_i = p/m_i`
    73	  pairwise coprime, `gcd(D_i, kappa) = 1` (`(C-2)`, `(C-3)`);
    74	* `p, q >= 2`, `gcd(p, q) = 1` (cross-side coprimality of cone orders
    75	  is then free);
    76	* CUSP-PARITY: some `eps in {±1}` with `(-1)^{N-s} = eps^q` and
    77	  `(-1)^{N-s'} = eps^p`, realised by a partition of `W` into parts
    78	  `>= 2` (7.B: `mu_l >= 2`) via `eps = (-1)^{W - n_cyc}`.
    79	  Realisability: `W = 2` forces `eps = -1`; `W = 3` forces `eps = +1`;
    80	  `W >= 4` both. In particular `j = N-2` admits only `eps = -1`.
    81	
    82	Both-unbounded (`s = s' = 1`) is empty: `p` and `q` are both multiples
    83	of `M >= 2`. `(C-4)` is the identification of `s, s'` with cycle counts
    84	of `rho(alpha), rho(beta)`, so the implied cycle types are
    85	`alpha ~ (m_i kappa)_i`, `beta ~ (l_j kappa)_j`.
    86	
    87	A **pair** is a unique `(p, q)`. A **tuple** is
    88	`(p, q, j, M, kappa, s, s', alpha-type, beta-type, a, mer, eps)`.
    89	Unbounded `D`-families are truncated only for listing; the exact
    90	objects are the finite cells plus the arithmetic progressions of §5.
    91	
    92	This is the numerical cage. The representation gate (transitivity,
    93	meridian type, `cover_h1` torsion-free of rank `j`, COR 7.2
    94	nonregular) is run on N <= 8 and on selected N = 9 cells; it is **not**
    95	claimed for N >= 10.
