   278	  `a_p = 1` (MI Prop. 6.1). `(C3)`: `#{K_p > 0} <= R + beta` with
   279	  `beta = 1` is `1 <= R + 1`, free.
   280	  The one sharp kill: mer `(3,3)` read as two dicriticals each
   281	  `s_l = 1`. Lemma 4.3 (each `s_l = 1` contributes `k_t >= 1` at the
   282	  NI place) plus additivity of `K_p` gives `K_p >= 2`, against
   283	  `a - 1 = 1`. So the two-birational reading is dead.
   284	  The single-dicritical reading `(2, 3)` has `R=1`, `K_p=1`, compatible
   285	  with RH on a degree-2 map `A^1 -> A^1`.
