   121	
   122	### 2.1 The identity, restated exactly, with its hypotheses
   123	
   124	`(M')`'s block-free form is quoted by REP96 SS7 R4 from its source `[S]` SS7:
   125	
   126	> Each irreducible component `D_i` has its own constant `a^{(i)} >= 1` on
   127	> `D_i \ Sing(D)`, and
   128	> `sum_i a^{(i)} chi_c(D_i \ Sing D) + sum_{p in Sing D} a_p = 1 - d chi_c(V)`.
   129	
   130	Objects: `d = N`; `V = C^2 \ A_F`, so `chi_c(V) = 1 - chi_c(A_F)`;
   131	`a^{(i)} = #F^{-1}(pt)` on `D_i \ Sing(A_F)`, constant there by the block-free
   132	covering lemma; `a_p = #F^{-1}(p)`. It is the stratification
   133	`chi_c(F^{-1}(A_F)) = sum_i a^{(i)} chi_c(D_i \ Sing D) + sum_p a_p` set against
   134	the Keller-only Euler budget (E), `chi_c(F^{-1}(A_F)) = 1 - N chi_c(V)`. Only
   135	Keller is used; `(H2)`+`(H3)` are what collapse it to a single `a`.
   136	
   137	*Control that the reading is right.* Under `(H2)`+`(H3)`: `m = 1`, `chi~ = 1`,
   138	`chi_c(D \ Sing D) = 1 - nu - s`, `a^{(1)} = a`, and the display becomes
   139	`a(nu + s - 1) - sum_p a_p = N nu - 1`, verbatim `(M')`. `[A]`
   140	
   141	### 2.2 THEOREM COLLAPSE-N
   142	
   143	Write `Sigma := Sing(A_F)`, `sigma := |Sigma|`, `sigma_i := |Sigma n D_i|`,
   144	`r_{i,p} := #eta_i^{-1}(p)` (zero off `D_i`),
   145	`nu_i := sum_{p in Sigma n D_i}(r_{i,p} - 1)`, `chi~_i := chi_c(D~_i)`. Every
   146	correction site lies in `Sigma` (a critical point of `eta_i` makes `D_i` singular),
   147	so `sum_{p in Sigma} K_p = K_tot`.
   148	
   149	> **THEOREM COLLAPSE-N `[D]`.** Assume only: each `D~_i` is smooth irreducible
   150	> with `chi_c(D~_i) = chi~_i`, `a^{(i)} = N - W_i`, and `(LOC)`
   151	> `a_p + sum_i r_{i,p} W_i + K_p = N` at every `p in Sigma`. Then
   152	>
   153	> ```text
   154	>    LHS(M'-bf) - RHS(M'-bf) = (N - 1) - K_tot - sum_i W_i chi~_i .
   155	> ```
   156	>
   157	> Hence `(M'-bf)` holds **iff** `sum_i W_i chi~_i + K_tot = N - 1`. Granted the
   158	> Orevkov budget `(AGG)` `sum_i W_i + K_tot = N - 1`, this is equivalent to
   159	> `sum_i W_i (chi~_i - 1) = 0`, i.e. - since `W_i >= 1` and `chi~_i <= 1` for any
   160	> smooth affine curve - to `chi~_i = 1` for every `i`, which is Lemma A.
   161	
   162	*Proof.* `eta_i` is injective off `eta_i^{-1}(Sigma)`, so
   163	`chi_c(D_i \ Sigma) = chi~_i - sum_{p in Sigma} r_{i,p} = chi~_i - sigma_i - nu_i`,
   164	and `chi_c(A_F) = sum_i (chi~_i - sigma_i - nu_i) + sigma`. Summing `(LOC)` over
   165	`Sigma` and using `sum_{p in Sigma} r_{i,p} = sigma_i + nu_i`,
   166	
   167	```text
   168	   sum_{p in Sigma} a_p = N sigma - sum_i W_i (sigma_i + nu_i) - K_tot .
   169	```
   170	
   171	Substitute both into the left side, with `a^{(i)} = N - W_i`:
   172	
   173	```text
   174	LHS = sum_i (N - W_i)(chi~_i - sigma_i - nu_i)
   175	        + N sigma - sum_i W_i (sigma_i + nu_i) - K_tot
   176	    = sum_i (N - W_i) chi~_i - N sum_i (sigma_i + nu_i) + N sigma - K_tot ,
   177	```
   178	
   179	the `W_i (sigma_i + nu_i)` terms cancelling in pairs. The right side is
   180	
   181	```text
   182	RHS = 1 - N chi_c(V) = 1 - N + N chi_c(A_F)
   183	    = 1 - N + N sum_i chi~_i - N sum_i (sigma_i + nu_i) + N sigma .
   184	```
   185	
   186	Subtract: the two `-N sum_i (sigma_i + nu_i)` and the two `N sigma` cancel, and
   187	`sum_i (N - W_i) chi~_i - N sum_i chi~_i = - sum_i W_i chi~_i`, leaving
   188	`LHS - RHS = (N - 1) - K_tot - sum_i W_i chi~_i`. []
   189	
   190	**Every singularity variable has vanished** - `sigma_i`, `nu_i`, `sigma`, the
   191	split of `Sigma` into self-singularities and crossings, the `r_{i,p}`, the node
   192	counts of *all* components. The identity's entire content on the cage is one scalar
   193	equation in `(W_i, chi~_i, K_tot, N)`.
   194	
   195	### 2.3 The general-N analogue of `chi_2 + sigma_2 = 1`, per profile
   196	
   197	Task (1) asks for the exact per-profile analogue. It is COLLAPSE-N, and it is the
   198	*same* equation on every profile:
   199	
   200	```text
   201	   (2.1)    sum_i W_i (chi~_i - 1) = 0 ,   equivalently   chi~_i = 1 for all i.
   202	```
   203	
   204	Componentwise, `chi~_i = 1` reads `chi_c(D_i) + (self-branch excess) = 1`; for a
   205	component whose only singularities are `sigma_i^{self}` nodes it is literally
   206	`chi_i + sigma_i^{self} = 1`. **REP96's (7.1) is exactly the `i = 2` instance of
   207	(2.1)**, and it looked like a constraint on `D_2` only because Lemma A had already
   208	been spent on `D_1` and the remaining unknown was solved for; fixing `D_2`'s
   209	normalisation first, the same algebra would have "constrained" `D_1` and cancelled
   210	`sigma_2`. There is no branched/companion asymmetry in `(M')` and no
   211	profile-dependence. Uniformly at every `N` and every ledger row:
   212	
   213	| question | answer from COLLAPSE-N |
   214	|---|---|
   215	| does the branched component's singularity data always cancel? | **yes**, identically, at every `N`, on every profile |
   216	| does the companion's cancel too? | **yes** - the charge's premise that `(M')` "constrains only `D_2`" is an artefact of the order of substitution |
   217	| what does `(M')` force on the companion: genus, `chi`, node count, crossings `j` with `D_1`? | **genus and `chi~` only**: `g_i = 0` and one place at infinity, i.e. Lemma A. Node count: nothing. `j`: nothing |
   218	| exact analogue of `chi_2 + sigma_2 = 1` per profile | (2.1), profile-independent |
   219	
   220	### 2.4 Why the same identity is fatal under (H2) and inert here
   221	
   222	REP96 SS7 R4's control - no nodal `N = 4` residual survives `(M')` under `(H2)` -
   223	is correct, and the diagnosis matters. The kill does not come from the identity but
   224	from combining it with **inequalities**: `a_p >= 0` and the ceiling `a <= N-2`.
   225	Prop 2.4 `[S]` proves the latter as
   226	`sigma = a + b_box = N - sum_{j: e_j>=2} delta_j e_j <= N - 2`, at the stated scope
   227	*every component of `A_F` lying in the branch locus* - the subtraction needs a
   228	ramified dicritical over that very component. So in RED-N the ceiling is
   229	
   230	```text
   231	   a^{(i)} <= N - 2   for branched D_i    <=>   W_i >= 2   for branched D_i,
   232	```
   233	
   234	which is automatic (`W_i >= mu_l >= 2`), and it is **not** available on companions:
   235	`a^{(companion)} = N - w` can be `N - 1`. This is a genuine flag/place separation -
   236	"component of `A_F`" is not "branch component" - and mis-applying Prop 2.4 to a
   237	companion would kill the promoted `N = 4` profile `W = (1,2)` outright and falsely.
   238	`[A]` **AUDIT-CC-1.**
   239	
   240	With the ceiling neutralised, all that is left of `(M')` in RED-N is `a_p >= 0` and
   241	`a_p <= a^{(i)}`. Both are *consequences* of `(LOC)`:
   242	`a_p = N - sum_j r_{j,p}W_j - K_p >= 0` is (LOC-1)/(LOC-2), and
   243	`a_p <= N - r_{i,p}W_i <= N - W_i = a^{(i)}` is automatic. So:
   244	
   245	> **Corollary `[D]`.** In scope RED-N, the entire content of `(M')` - identity,
   246	> ceiling and fibre bounds - is implied by `(LOC)` + `(AGG)` + Lemma A, all three
   247	> promoted. `(M')` is not an independent gate in the reducible branch.
   248	
   249	This independently reproduces, and extends from `(AGG)` to the unequal-`a^{(i)}`
   250	form of `(M')`, N5 SS1.4's finding that the aggregate Euler identity carries no
   251	information beyond the Orevkov budget with the local fibre identities. `[A]`
   252	
