   283	## 3. The forced companion datum at general N
   284	
   285	### 3.1 What a companion is
   286	
   287	Fix a profile from the CAGE-N-R2 ledger. A component `D_i` is **branched** iff it
   288	owns a carrier with `mu_l >= 2`; there are `b_br` of these, `1 <= b_br <=
   289	floor((N-2)/2)`. Every other component - call it a **companion** - owns only
   290	trivial carriers `(1,1,0)`, so with `w_i := #{trivials on D_i}`:
   291	
   292	```text
   293	   W_i = w_i ,   a^{(i)} = N - w_i ,   K_i = 0 ,   iota_i = 0 ,
   294	   meridian gamma_i of cycle type 1^{a_i} prod 1^{s_l} = 1^N  (trivial).
   295	```
   296	
   297	At `N = 4,5` `(RC2)` forces `b_br = 1`; at `N >= 6` a profile can have `b_br = 2`
   298	or `3`, and the notion stays well defined per component. Companions are exactly the
   299	components carrying no monodromy - hence invisible to the whole `pi_1` layer, and
   300	attackable only through curve geometry.
   301	
   302	### 3.2 The complete forced datum
   303	
   304	Every clause below is promoted or is derived here from promoted material; the
