   344	*(i) The pin is sharper.* `(A,B)` is the **same** for every component; only `m`
   345	varies. The one remaining freedom `xi -> lambda xi` sends
   346	`(A,B) -> (A lambda^{md}, B lambda^{me})` and fixes `A^e/B^d`. So the
   347	component-independent scalar is `A^e/B^d`, and it equals the invariant of the
   348	leading forms, `P_+^e = (A^e/B^d) Q_+^d`, the relation the Jacobian condition
   349	forces. This is strictly stronger than "the ratio `deg p_i/deg q_i` is the same".
