   499	### 4.3 Consequence, and the exact answer to the charge
   500	
   501	> **Corollary `[D]`.** For every `N >= 4`, every profile in the CAGE-N-R2 ledger,
   502	> and every companion slot of weight `w` in it, the forced companion datum
   503	> (C1)-(C8) is realized by an explicit curve at every multiplicity `m` not excluded
   504	> by MULT-2. C5 constrains only `w`, a property of the profile and not of the
   505	> curve; C9 is a finite set of open conditions relative to the rest of `A_F`; C10
   506	> and C11 are vacuous on companions (SS3.5 (N2), THEOREM COLLAPSE-N). **There is no
   507	> `N_0 >= 4` beyond which the companion datum is contradictory**, and the only
   508	> exclusion found anywhere in the lane is MULT-2's `m = 1` at `min(d,e) = 1`, which
   509	> is a constraint on the multiplicity, not on the degree.
