+The campaign is not one theorem from closure in the operational sense. It is
+one named theorem from making the **A2 analytic subproblem finite**, while the
+same `H2` branch still contains three other unbounded profile species and the
+complement of `H2` has a realized companion datum. Here `H2` means exactly
+“`A_F` is irreducible” `[M:26-30]`; its complement is the reducible
+nonproperness curve, not a neglected subcase of the horn. The all-degree
+profile theorem proves real structural progress—smooth is empty at every `N`,
+smooth-branch profiles are empty through `N=16`, and the residual is precisely
+(A), (B2), (B3), then (B1) from `N=17` `[M:413-438]`—but it also proves that a
+bounded-`N` architecture cannot finish: the first legal (B1) profile occurs at
+`N=17` and legal profiles persist `[M:376-394]`.
