+## 8. Detailed idea cards
+
+### Card 1 — `FULL-EO / SL2-TERMINATION`
+
+**Dependencies.** The source quotient and exact even/odd bracket equations; an
+explicit map to the ray variables; the legal normalizations and open factors;
+the `SL_2(C[Z])` residue reduction; fraction-free block elimination.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.** Derive the generic newest-block matrix including
+O0/O1 and determine whether its maximal minors vanish identically for
+`t=(U-3e-2)/2>0`. Specialize only after the symbolic branch split.
+
+**Outcome interpretation.** A universally nonzero minor or forced `H'=0` is a
+uniform proof lead. An identically deficient block yields a recurrence kernel
+for the shooter. A terminating full solution is `FULL_EO_POINT`, not yet an
+admissible pullback. A missing map or vanished leader is `OPEN`.
+
+**Stop condition.** Stop Mason-only work and monotone cells once the full generic
+block is classified; stop construction at the first failed admissibility arrow.
+
+**Expected information gain.** **Extreme.** The same calculation decides
+whether the live infinity is obstruction, recurrence, or gauge and points in
+the correct proof/disproof direction.
+
+### Card 2 — `GAMMA-B3-REGRESSION -> N6`
+
+The bank already contains
+
+```text
+Gamma: y^2=x^3(x-1)^2,       t |-> (t^2,t^3(t^2-1)).
+```
+
+It is birational with normalization `A1`, has exactly a `(2,3)` cusp at `t=0`
+and one transverse node from `t=+-1`, and no other affine singularity
+(`xmodel/block-descent-a1-quartic-cycle1-pseudoplane-companion-threat-map-sol56-20260830.md:355-387`).
+Thus it is an exact curve-level realization of the simplest B3 singularity
+shape (`k=1`), a new cross-connection to the freshly pinned B3 cage.
+
+**Dependencies.** A complete generic-projection critical-value census for
+`Gamma`; native ZvK braids in both orientations; all transposition tuples in
+`S_4`; B3's required cusp `(3,1)` and node `(2,2)` partitions; the repaired
+global cover-homology checker.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.** Run the full native factorization and, for each
+survivor, compute the index-four subgroup's `H_1` and the push-off action. B3
+predicts for `k=1` an irreducible rational `E` with five places at infinity
+`[HF:333-349]`.
+
+**Outcome interpretation.** Native zero kills this curve only. Torsion in the
+global subgroup homology kills that curve/representation as a plane-source
+cover directly—this is not NO-PUSHFORWARD. A torsion-free survivor is a
+cover-level regression success and goes to source-open completion. Because
+`N=4` is already impossible, the first failing global condition is a candidate
+uniform B3 invariant to test at `N=6`; no new `N=4` proof is sought.
+
+**Stop condition.** One fully audited `Gamma` run, then either generalize the
+identified invariant to `N=6` or stop. Do not enumerate more degree-four
+curves.
+
+**Expected information gain.** **High mechanism value, zero direct frontier
+closure.** It gives the B3 theory an actual curve while respecting the accepted
+low-degree foundation.
+
+### Card 3 — `PRIME-7-SCOUT / PROFILE-FIRST-CENSUS`
+
+**Dependencies.** The exact H2 profile at `N=7`, separate B2/B3 presentations,
+faithful curve encodings, and an explicit check of covering degree,
+transitivity, and whether the local meridian really is a transposition.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.** Before the composite `S_6` realization farm, fix
+one meridian modulo conjugacy and enumerate `N=7` relation/cycle-type tuples
+with incremental Schreier–Sims. Prime-degree transitivity gives primitivity;
+only branches actually containing a transposition may then be pinned to `S_7`.
+Case (A) and B1 are already absent at `N=7`, leaving B2/B3.
+
+**Outcome interpretation.** Zero is a presentation/profile screen unless
+coverage is proved, never an `N=7` theorem by itself. Survivors identify curve
+families and relation types worth realizing, and their pattern can simplify
+the harder composite `N=6` search. A non-transposition branch remains in its
+actual subgroup class; it is not promoted to `S_7`.
+
+**Stop condition.** Stop at a complete representation classification and
+launch at most the first two faithful curve families. If it does not reduce the
+curve queue, return to `N=6` directly.
+
+**Expected information gain.** **Medium-high at desk cost.** It prices the
+group-theoretic scaling before expensive curve realization without pretending
+that prime `7` closes the first open degree `6`.
