+   residual O0/O1 rows from this source and exhibit the ring/image map into the
+   ray variables. If that map cannot be written, return typed `OPEN`.
+2. On the residue line, factor the `SL_2(C[Z])` matrix of Section 4 and expose
+   its common partial quotient `H`. Substitute before expansion. This separates
+   genuine terminal data from the arbitrary Bezout/continued-fraction freedom.
+3. At a generic top `A`-level, form the coefficient matrix on only the newest
+   coefficient block, over `Q(e,U,j)` with order index `j`. Compute its maximal
+   minors fraction-free and branch on every vanished pivot. The existing formal
+   theorem says bottom-up levels are always solvable with one free `C[Z]`
+   parameter; therefore a proof must come from the terminal boundary, not from
+   another low-order obstruction
+   (`xmodel/one-cusp-a2-r2-opus5-20260901.md:188-237`).
+4. Prove one of two exact statements: either a pivot/terminal polynomial is
+   nonzero for every `t>0`, forcing `H'=0` and `U=3e+2`; or every exceptional
+   factor forces a previously killed chamber/wall. Then the finite-cell engine
+   is licensed. If the generic block remains deficient, the proof attack has
+   falsified its own premise and hands the kernel to the construction attack.
+
+Controls are the exact-empty `(1,3)` and `(1,5)` cells, the boundary theorem
+`U=3e`, and a deliberately wrong wall sign. A finite list of empty `U` values is
+never an outcome of this proof attack. Even a uniform A2 kill closes only the
+declared A-degree-two obstruction layer, not B3, cusp-(A), B2, B1, the reducible
