+## 4. New mechanism and cross-connection
+
+### `A2-SL2-DESCENT` — a genuinely new mechanism
+
+On a live ray cell, `[RK]` declares
+
+```text
+n = U-e,       sigma = (U+e)/2,
+deg q = U,     deg s = sigma,
+deg r' = n-1,  deg p' = 3n/2-1,
+2(q r' - p' s) = kappa != 0.
+```
+
+Here `p'` and `r'` are source **variable labels**, not derivatives; below every
+derivative is written `partial_Z`.
+
+Thus
+
+```text
+             [ q   p' ]
+M(Z) =       [ s   r' ]       has det M = kappa/2 in C*.
+```
+
+This is not an analogy: after a constant rescaling, `M` is an element of
+`SL_2(C[Z])`. On every surviving cell `U>=3e+2`, the two degree differences are
+the same nonnegative integer
+
+```text
+t := deg(p')-deg(q) = deg(r')-deg(s) = (U-3e-2)/2.
+```
+
+Moreover
+
+```text
+r'/s - p'/q = kappa/(2qs).
+```
+
+The right side is strictly proper at infinity, so the polynomial parts of
+`p'/q` and `r'/s` coincide. Call that common quotient `H(Z)`, `deg H=t`, and
+write
+
+```text
+p' = Hq + p_0,       r' = Hs + r_0.
+```
+
+Then `q r_0-p_0 s=kappa/2`; equivalently the elementary column operation
+`C_2 <- C_2-H C_1` preserves the unit determinant and strictly reduces the
+second column. Repeating the Euclidean algorithm gives a continued-
+fraction/elementary-matrix word for `M`. `E0` alone permits arbitrary word
+length; any Mason–Stothers bound must therefore consume other equations.
+
+There is a sharper finite test than a generic coefficient hunt. Choose the
+unique reduced Bezout complement `(p_0,r_0)` and rename `H=Lambda`. Direct
+substitution in the source-derived O0/O1 equations gives
+
+```text
+A0 = s C1 - q E1
+B0 = 4(C1 r_0 - p_0 E1) + 2(q partial_Z(s) - partial_Z(q) s)
+A1 = s C2 - q E2
+B1 = 8(C2 r_0 - p_0 E2)
+     + 4(C1 partial_Z(E1) - partial_Z(C1) E1)
+     + 6 D1 partial_Z(s) - 2 partial_Z(D1) s
+     + 4 Z(q partial_Z(s) - partial_Z(q) s),
+O0 = B0 + 4 A0 Lambda = 0,
+O1 = B1 + 8 A1 Lambda = 0.
+```
+
+Hence every full solution satisfies the compatibility and divisibility tests
+
+```text
+K := A0 B1 - 2 A1 B0 = 0,       A0 divides B0,
+Lambda = -B0/(4A0).
+```
+
+On RAY-2, the declared top coefficients make `deg A0=U+2e` and
+`deg A1=U+2e+1`; neither denominator branch can be discarded as “possibly
+zero” (`xmodel/cell-32-spec-sol56-20260901.md:82-114`; `[RK]`). Substitute the
+wall and top-two ray pins into `K`, then compute `rem(B0,A0)` first at `(1,5)`,
+`(1,7)`, and `(2,8)`. A first nonzero coefficient kills that branch; a finite
+root set bounds `U` on it; an identity plus nonzero remainder exposes the next
+recurrence; and identities for both are a formal-family signal only. Only
+after this discriminator should the lane collect the remaining EQ1–EQ4/T1
+coefficients or recurse on further elementary quotients.
+
+This cross-connects Avenue 29's Hamiltonian identities with Avenue 5's
+Jung/elementary descent at an exact one-variable PID client. It also enforces
+the raw-degree guardrail: an elementary factorization of `M` is not yet a legal
+source or target automorphism of `F`. The lane must exhibit the map from the
+matrix column operation to the original normal-form variables before declaring
+`U` gauge.
+
+### Safe analytic/group bridge
+
+Do not identify the A2 cell and B3 curve by their shared “horn” label. First
+produce `OPEN[A2-TO-B3-OBJECT-MAP]`: from a full analytic solution, output the
+actual divisor or boundary valuation representing `A_F` and the pullback
+`E=F^{-1}(A_F)`. Only then compare the signature
+
+```text
+(#components(E), genus(normalization(E)), #places_infinity(E),
+ local branch types, cover cycle types).
+```
+
+At `N=4`, B3 predicts this signature exactly in terms of the number and parity
+of double-point contacts `[HF:315-349]`, whereas the explicit A2 source chart
+under its rank-four hypothesis has geometric degree eight. Those are not
+comparable objects as currently written. If a future route lands in the same
+degree and profile, a mismatch kills that routed cell and a match merely
+licenses construction. Without the divisor-valued route, the bridge remains
+typed `OPEN`, not filled by the packet's “same object” wording.
