+## 1. Executive thesis and reframing
+
+The campaign is one theorem from making the **A2 subproblem finite**, not one
+theorem from JC2. `H2` means exactly that `A_F` is irreducible `[M:26-30]`; its
+complement is reducible `A_F`. Under H2, smooth is empty at all `N`, B1 is empty
+through 16, but (A), (B2), (B3), and B1 from 17 remain `[M:413-438]`. Thus no
+bounded-`N` architecture can finish.
+
+I reframe the frontier around two questions. First, is A2's `U` geometric
+complexity or merely the length of a unimodular/continued-fraction
+presentation? Second, can any survivor traverse a declared state arrow—cell to
+analytic pullback, curve representation to global cover/source, or companion
+curve to jointly realized reducible `A_F`? Standalone companion data are
+attained by curves and still imply no map `[CC:499-525]`.
+
+Put the cofinal ceiling and state arrows ahead of more bounded cages. On the
+positive side, lift the A2 ray by a finite recurrence or realize an actual
+`N>=6` curve-cover package. The rigid `N=4` B3 object is only a known-impossible
+regression fixture; accepted `N<=5` closure forbids treating it as a CE target.
