+## 6. Strongest counterexample / falsification attack
+
+Run the same full system in the opposite direction as
+`A2-TERMINATION-SHOOTER`.
+
+The reason this outranks an undifferentiated `S_6` search is proximity to an
+actual map. Every immersive residue datum satisfying
+`2(qr'-p's)=kappa` has an all-order formal solution, with a free polynomial at
+each `A`-level; the sole issue is finite termination
+(`xmodel/one-cusp-a2-r2-opus5-20260901.md:195-237`). Start from a declared last
+nonzero `A`-level and solve the full `E/O` recurrence **backward** toward the
+residue, while the `SL_2` word parameterizes the residue freedom. Equivalently,
+treat it as a two-boundary shooting problem: prescribed ray at `A=0`, zero tail
+at level `D+1`.
+
+The state ladder is mandatory:
+
+```text
+SUBSYSTEM_POINT
+  -> FULL_EO_POINT in the declared quotient R
+  -> ADMISSIBLE_PULLBACK (all opens, boundary/general-fibre data,
+                          and [K:C(f,g)]=4 checked)
+  -> POLYNOMIAL_KELLER_PAIR under the explicit source chart
+  -> COUNTEREXAMPLE only after noninvertibility/geometric degree is certified.
+```
+
+The explicit chart
+`A=x^2, U=x+x^3y, Z=2y+x^2y^2` carries a full quotient solution to a polynomial
+pair with constant Jacobian. Under the separately checked rank-four condition,
+the resulting geometric degree is `2*4=8`; this is why a terminating admissible
+solution is counterexample-level rather than another representation
+(`xmodel/theta-reopen-explicit-pullback-sol56-20260831.md:412-449`). None of
+those later arrows may be inferred from a residual cell.
+
+Outcomes are deliberately symmetric. A nonzero terminal obstruction becomes
+the strongest proof lemma. An identically deficient full-system block yields a
+constructive recurrence; the first terminating orbit is checked directly in
+`R`, then through the source chart. A nonterminating formal orbit is only a
+formal object. Failure to derive O0/O1 or a branch with a vanished leader is
+typed `OPEN`, not silently discarded.
+
+In parallel but second priority, build the `N=6` census around actual curves.
+`N=4` B3 is only a known-impossible regression laboratory—`N<=5` is closed and
+must not be re-hardened—not a counterexample target. Its value is to force any
+proposed group-to-geometry bridge to find the missing obstruction before that
+bridge is trusted at `N=6`.
