+### `FIXED-MERIDIAN-SPAN` (`EXACT-DESK / UNREVIEWED`)
+
+In case (A), let `Y=C^2\E`, `H=pi_1(Y)`, and let `m` be a positive generic
+meridian of `A_F`. For every sheet `v` fixed by `rho(m)`, lift `m` to a loop
+`ell_v in H`. Then necessarily
+
+```text
+<[ell_v] : v in Fix rho(m)> = H_1(Y;Z).
+```
+
+Indeed each irreducible component `E_i` dominates `A_F`; over a generic smooth
+point, étaleness identifies one local sheet on `E_i` and its lifted loop with
+the positive component meridian. These meridians form the basis of
+`H_1(C^2\E)=Z^j` `[HT:95-107]`. This is global case-(A) geometry, not a
+local-to-global torsion push: here the torus-knot group is already the global
+complement group `[HT:342-365]`. Thus
+`Q(rho):=H_1(H)/<[ell_v]>` must vanish.
+
+An independent Schreier/SNF replay reproduced the charged fixed-orientation
+counts; mirrors follow by swapping generators. For all 16 trefoil reps,
+`H_1(H)=Z^2` but adjoining the two fixed-meridian rows leaves `Q=Z`; for all six
+`(3,4)` reps, `H_1(H)=Z^3` and four fixed rows again leave `Q=Z`. On the family
+`(3,4D)`, `D` odd and `3∤D`, the banked meridian claim has a correction:
+`D≡5 mod 6` gives an 8-cycle and no fixed sheet, while `D≡1 mod 6` has the
+required four fixed sheets but still `Q=Z`; mirrors agree.
+
+Route this immediately to different-model replay. Controls: original rep counts
+and H1 ranks before augmentation, multiple Schreier trees, simultaneous
+conjugacy, shifted Bezout pairs, mirror swap, and the exact `N=1` positive
+control `det([[p,-q],[e,f]])=pf+qe=1`, hence `Q=0`. A confirmed `Q!=0` kills
+only the enumerated representation; completeness of the case-(A) census is
+separately required before closing N8. `Q=0` would be necessary only, never
