+## 7. Software acceleration and decisive experiment
+
+### `BLOCK-RECURRENCE`
+
+Replace whole-cell Gröbner expansion by a source-derived sparse top-down
+eliminator. The current subsystem has
+
+```text
+variables  = (9U+5e)/2 + 6,
+generators = (15U+19e)/2 + 5,
+```
+
+so even `(e,U)=(1,5)` is already 31 variables / 52 generators
+(`xmodel/a2-cells-codegen-sol56-20260902.md:70-93`). Yet each order introduces
+only a small block of new coefficients, linearly. The program should:
+
+1. generate full `E=kappa,O=0` directly in the ordered quotient ring, then
+   verify the residual variable map coefficientwise;
+2. reduce the residue `SL_2` matrix and retain the partial quotient `H`
+   symbolically;
+3. perform fraction-free row reduction of the newest block over
+   `Q(e,U,j)`, emitting every pivot numerator as an exceptional branch;
+4. send only exceptional residual ideals to `qqideal`/`msolve`, with explicit
+   Rabinowitsch variables and no `sat()` wrapper;
+5. output either `GENERIC_TERMINAL_OBSTRUCTION`, `RECURRENCE_KERNEL`, or typed
+   `OPEN[vanished leader/ring map]`, plus the source-to-output map.
+
+Smallest useful test: reproduce exact EMPTY for `(1,3)` and `(1,5)`, reproduce
+RAY-EDGE on `(2,6)`, make a wrong wall sign fail the expected coefficient
+check, and preserve a planted full-system point. One generic nonzero pivot
+polynomial would be more informative than dozens of cells; an identically zero
+pivot supplies the construction kernel. Stop extending the monotone `U` window
+after the jobs already queued—no finite window can certify a cap
+(`[RK:427-434,480-489]`).
