+## 5. Strongest proof attack
+
+### `FIXED-MERIDIAN-SPAN` (`EXACT-DESK / UNREVIEWED`)
+
+In case (A), let `Y=C^2\E`, `H=pi_1(Y)`, and let `m` be a positive generic
+meridian of `A_F`. For every sheet `v` fixed by `rho(m)`, lift `m` to a loop
+`ell_v in H`. Then necessarily
+
+```text
+<[ell_v] : v in Fix rho(m)> = H_1(Y;Z).
+```
+
+Indeed each irreducible component `E_i` dominates `A_F`: if `F|E_i` were
+constant, its tangent would lie in `ker(dF)`, contradicting `det JF!=0`. Over a
+generic smooth point, étaleness identifies a local sheet on `E_i` and its
+lifted loop with the positive component meridian. These meridians form the
+basis of `H_1(C^2\E;Z)=Z^j` `[HT:95-107]`. This only says every basis class
+occurs among the fixed lifts; it neither identifies fixed sheets with
+components nor excludes repeated or infinity sheets. This is global case-(A)
+geometry, not a local-to-global torsion push: the torus-knot group is already
+the global complement group `[HT:342-365]`. Thus
+`Q(rho):=H_1(H;Z)/<[ell_v]>` must vanish.
+
+An independent Schreier/SNF replay reproduced the charged fixed-orientation
+counts; mirrors follow by swapping generators. For all 16 trefoil reps,
+`H_1(H)=Z^2` but adjoining the two fixed-meridian rows leaves `Q=Z`; for all six
+`(3,4)` reps, `H_1(H)=Z^3` and four fixed rows again leave `Q=Z`. On the family
+`(3,4D)`, `D` odd and `3∤D`, the banked meridian claim has a correction:
+every `D≡5 mod 6` gives an 8-cycle and fails `a=4`, while every charged
+`D<=49` sample with `D≡1 mod 6` has four fixed sheets and `Q=Z`; no symbolic
+all-`D` SNF claim is made. The Bezout words are `alpha beta^-1` for `D=6k+1`
+and `alpha^2 beta^3` for `D=6k+5`; each SNF uses the actual relator
+`alpha^3 beta^(-4D)`, and mirrors use the generator swap.
+
+Route this immediately to different-model replay. Controls: original rep counts
+and H1 ranks before augmentation, multiple Schreier trees, simultaneous
+conjugacy, shifted Bezout pairs, mirror swap, and the exact `N=1` positive
+control `det([[p,-q],[e,f]])=pf+qe=1`, hence `Q=0`. A confirmed `Q!=0` kills
+only the enumerated representation; completeness of the case-(A) census is
+separately required before closing N8. `Q=0` would be necessary only, never
+attainment. Meanwhile `FULL-EO/SL2-TOP-DOWN` remains the strongest A2 proof
+experiment described in Sections 4 and 7.
+
+## 6. Strongest counterexample / falsification attack
+
+Run the same full system in the opposite direction as
+`A2-TERMINATION-SHOOTER`.
+
+The reason this outranks an undifferentiated `S_6` search is proximity to an
+actual map. Every immersive residue datum satisfying
+`2(qr'-p's)=kappa` has an all-order formal solution, with a free polynomial at
+each `A`-level; the sole issue is finite termination
+(`xmodel/one-cusp-a2-r2-opus5-20260901.md:195-237`). Start from a declared last
+nonzero `A`-level and solve the full `E/O` recurrence **backward** toward the
+residue, while the `SL_2` word parameterizes the residue freedom. Equivalently,
+treat it as a two-boundary shooting problem: prescribed ray at `A=0`, zero tail
+at level `D+1`.
+
+The state ladder is mandatory:
+
+```text
+SUBSYSTEM_POINT
+  -> FULL_EO_POINT in the declared quotient R
+  -> ADMISSIBLE_PULLBACK (all opens, boundary/general-fibre data,
+                          and [K:C(f,g)]=4 checked)
+  -> POLYNOMIAL_KELLER_PAIR under the explicit source chart
+  -> COUNTEREXAMPLE only after noninvertibility/geometric degree is certified.
+```
+
+The explicit chart
+`A=x^2, U=x+x^3y, Z=2y+x^2y^2` carries a full quotient solution to a polynomial
+pair with constant Jacobian. Under the separately checked rank-four condition,
+the resulting geometric degree is `2*4=8`; this is why a terminating admissible
+solution is counterexample-level rather than another representation
+(`xmodel/theta-reopen-explicit-pullback-sol56-20260831.md:412-449`). None of
+those later arrows may be inferred from a residual cell.
+
+Outcomes are deliberately symmetric. A nonzero terminal obstruction becomes
+the strongest proof lemma. An identically deficient full-system block yields a
+constructive recurrence; the first terminating orbit is checked directly in
+`R`, then through the source chart. A nonterminating formal orbit is only a
+formal object. Failure to derive O0/O1 or a branch with a vanished leader is
+typed `OPEN`, not silently discarded.
+
+In parallel but second priority, build the `N=6` census around actual curves.
+`N=4` B3 is only a known-impossible regression laboratory—`N<=5` is closed and
+must not be re-hardened—not a counterexample target. Its value is to force any
+proposed group-to-geometry bridge to find the missing obstruction before that
+bridge is trusted at `N=6`.
+
+## 7. Software acceleration and decisive experiment
+
+### `BLOCK-RECURRENCE`
+
+Replace whole-cell Gröbner expansion by a source-derived sparse top-down
+eliminator. The current subsystem has
+
+```text
+variables  = (9U+5e)/2 + 6,
+generators = (15U+19e)/2 + 5,
+```
+
+so even `(e,U)=(1,5)` is already 31 variables / 52 generators
+(`xmodel/a2-cells-codegen-sol56-20260902.md:70-93`). Yet each order introduces
+only a small block of new coefficients, linearly. The program should:
+
+1. generate full `E=kappa,O=0` directly in the ordered quotient ring, then
+   verify the residual variable map coefficientwise;
+2. reduce the residue `SL_2` matrix and retain the partial quotient `H`
+   symbolically;
+3. perform fraction-free row reduction of the newest block over
+   `Q(e,U,j)`, emitting every pivot numerator as an exceptional branch;
+4. send only exceptional residual ideals to `qqideal`/`msolve`, with explicit
+   Rabinowitsch variables and no `sat()` wrapper;
+5. output either `GENERIC_TERMINAL_OBSTRUCTION`, `RECURRENCE_KERNEL`, or typed
+   `OPEN[vanished leader/ring map]`, plus the source-to-output map.
+
+Smallest useful test: reproduce exact EMPTY for `(1,3)` and `(1,5)`, reproduce
+RAY-EDGE on `(2,6)`, make a wrong wall sign fail the expected coefficient
+check, and preserve a planted full-system point. One generic nonzero pivot
+polynomial would be more informative than dozens of cells; an identically zero
+pivot supplies the construction kernel. Stop extending the monotone `U` window
+after the jobs already queued—no finite window can certify a cap
+(`[RK:427-434,480-489]`).
+
+## 8. Detailed idea cards
+
+### Card 1 — `FULL-EO / SL2-TERMINATION`
+
+**Dependencies:** exact source `E/O`, ray ring map, legal opens, and the
+`SL_2(C[Z])` reduction. **Cheapest discriminator:** reduce `DET-EO` and then
+the exact `A0 | B0` remainder after the wall/top-two pins, before forming the
+full newest-coefficient block. **Outcomes:** a nonzero constant is a proof
+lead; discrete finite roots bound that branch; compatible identities expose
+the shooter recurrence, but a terminating solution is only `FULL_EO_POINT`;
+missing map/leader is `OPEN`. **Stop:** after the generic branch split—no more
+Mason-only or monotone-cell work. **Information gain:** **extreme**, because
+obstruction, recurrence, and presentation length separate in one calculation.
+
+### Card 2 — `GAMMA-B3-REGRESSION -> N6`
+
+The banked curve `Gamma:y^2=x^3(x-1)^2`, parametrized by
+`(t^2,t^3(t^2-1))`, has exactly a `(2,3)` cusp and one transverse node
+(`xmodel/block-descent-a1-quartic-cycle1-pseudoplane-companion-threat-map-sol56-20260830.md:355-387`): an exact curve-level B3 `k=1` control.
+**Dependencies:** complete projection census, native ZvK both orientations,
+all `S_4` tuples, and repaired global cover homology. **Cheapest discriminator:**
+full factorization, then index-four `H_1`; B3 predicts rational irreducible `E`
+with five ends `[HF:333-349]`. **Outcomes:** zero kills `Gamma` only; global
+torsion kills that curve/representation directly; torsion-free goes to
+source-open completion. The first failure is a candidate uniform `N=6` gate.
+**Stop:** one audited run, then generalize or archive—no more degree-four
+curves. **Information gain:** **high mechanism value, no direct closure**.
+
+### Card 3 — `PRIME-7-SCOUT / PROFILE-FIRST-CENSUS`
+
+**Dependencies:** exact `N=7` B2/B3 profiles, faithful encodings, and explicit
+degree/transitivity/transposition checks. **Cheapest discriminator:** fix a
+meridian up to conjugacy and enumerate with Schreier–Sims. Prime transitivity
+gives primitivity; only an actual transposition pins `S_7`. **Outcomes:** zero
+is a profile screen absent coverage; survivors select at most two curve
+families and can simplify composite `N=6`; other cycle types retain their real
+subgroups. **Stop:** after representation classification, or immediately if
+the `N=6` queue is not reduced. **Information gain:** **medium-high at desk
+cost**, never an `N=6` substitute.
+
+## 9. Current-lane decisions
+
+| Current lane | Call | Immediate instruction |
+|---|---|---|
+| `a2-ubound-opus5-20260902` | **continue, redesign first** | Source-derive O0/O1 and run generic top-block/`SL_2` descent before Mason or more instantiated elimination. If the full block stays deficient, hand its kernel to construction; if the ring map cannot be declared, return `OPEN`. |
+| `cusp-a-n8-gate-opus5-20260902` | **continue narrowly** | Start with the explicit order-24 trefoil cell and its actual index-eight subgroup. Compute marked meridian classes and a global Fox/Alexander module; NO-PUSHFORWARD forbids generic local-torsion rhetoric. Promote CUSP-A-KAPPA only after every normalizer branch is covered. |
+| `web-sweep-20260902-grok46` | **harvest, then stop** | Record only primary-source results with a direct live client. Queue post-freeze finds for their own gate; do not extend a threat-free broad sweep. |
+| box01 A2 cells | **finish queued window, then stop extension** | Preserve exact-Q/second-engine decisions as recurrence controls. Upgrade `(1,7)` if cheap and harvest `(1,9)`; no finite window implies a `U` bound. |
+| Box03 `869` | **stop at the existing cap** | Harvest a completed result, but do not relaunch or add fallback compute. It is confirmatory inside accepted `N=4` closure and nothing at the frontier depends on it. |
+
+## 10. Campaign-systems check
+
+### UPGRADE — make encoding faithfulness a hard launch gate
+
+The packet calls PREFLIGHT the tracked upgrade `[P:135-145]`; promote it from
+queued hygiene to a prerequisite for every `N>=6` realization job. This is not
+ceremonial: all six earlier nodal ideals used unfaithful raw/sliced coefficient
+conditions, including two apparent two-engine EMPTY results
+(`xmodel/encoding-faithfulness-audit-r2-sol56-20260901.md:189-215`).
+
+**Smallest useful test.** Before solver launch, the generator must (i) emit the
+reduced approximate root beside the ideal in the declared coefficient ring and
+order; (ii) exact-diff each encoded coefficient condition; (iii) make the old
+`(8,6,19)` false-positive canary fail the corrected `86A` cell; (iv) make the
+explicit four-node `(9,6,2)` curve pass corrected `96B`; and (v) fail closed on
+any ring, map, open-factor, or generator-order mismatch. The corrected ideals
+and semantic controls already exist
+`[xmodel/encoding-faithfulness-audit-r2-sol56-20260901.md:462-511]`.
+
+Add one output field, `state_level`, chosen from
+`NUMERICAL/REPRESENTATIVE/CURVE/FULL_COVER/ACTUAL_MAP`. A CI test must reject
+the known-invalid promotions “A2 cell -> B3 kill” and “local torsion -> global
+torsion”, while accepting “realized curve + complete native ZvK -> curve-level
+representation decision.” This small type check directly protects the new
+cross-front experiments.
+
+## 11. Allocation, falsifiers, and close
+
+Allocate frontier effort in this order: (1) full-source O0/O1 plus the generic
+block/`SL_2` discriminator; (2) the explicit case-(A) `N=8` global subgroup
+gate; (3) a preflighted profile-first `N=6` census, with the cheap prime-seven
+scout only if it reduces the curve queue; (4) one `Gamma` B3 regression; (5)
+joint companion/source-open completion only after a full cover survives.
+
+The portfolio changes direction on clear falsifiers. If the common quotient
+`H` is visible to the full equations but yields no uniform pivot, stop calling
+`U` gauge and run the construction recurrence. If a global N8 subgroup passes
+every marked/twisted test, switch that lane from exclusion to source-open
+construction. If the preflight cannot certify the curve encoding, launch no
+solver. If a degree-four regression merely fails at an already-known binding
+route, archive it rather than re-proving `N=4`.
+
+The central conclusion is deliberately negative about architecture: exact
+finite windows cannot resolve JC2. The next work must either expose a cofinal
+invariant or advance a survivor through a declared state arrow. Everything
+else is calibration.

