+## 5. Strongest proof attack
+
+### `FIXED-MERIDIAN-SPAN` (`EXACT-DESK / UNREVIEWED`)
+
+In case (A), let `Y=C^2\E`, `H=pi_1(Y)`, and let `m` be a positive generic
+meridian of `A_F`; H2+7.B gives `a=#Fix(rho(m))` `[HT:254-268]`. For each fixed
+sheet `v`, choose a Schreier word `t_v` so its based lift is
+`ell_v=t_v^-1 m t_v in H` in the declared action convention. Then necessarily
+
+```text
+<[ell_v] : v in Fix rho(m)> = H_1(Y;Z).
+```
+
+Indeed each irreducible component `E_i` dominates `A_F`: if `F|E_i` were
+constant, its tangent would lie in `ker(dF)`, contradicting `det JF!=0`. Over a
+generic smooth point, étaleness identifies a local sheet on `E_i` and its
+lifted loop with the positive component meridian. These meridians form the
+basis of `H_1(C^2\E;Z)=Z^j` `[HT:95-107]`. This only says every basis class
+occurs among the fixed lifts; it neither identifies fixed sheets with
+components nor excludes repetitions. This is global case-(A)
+geometry, not a local-to-global torsion push: the torus-knot group is already
+the global complement group `[HT:342-365]`. Thus
+`Q(rho):=H_1(H;Z)/<[ell_v]>` must vanish.
+
+An independent Schreier/SNF replay reproduced the charged fixed-orientation
+counts; mirrors follow by swapping generators. For all 16 trefoil reps,
+`H_1(H)=Z^2` but adjoining the two fixed-meridian rows leaves `Q=Z`; for all six
+`(3,4)` reps, `H_1(H)=Z^3` and four fixed rows again leave `Q=Z`. On the family
+`(3,4D)`, `D` odd and `3∤D`, an `EXACT-DESK / UNREVIEWED` candidate correction is:
+every `D≡5 mod 6` gives an 8-cycle and fails `a=4`, while every charged
+`D<=49` sample with `D≡1 mod 6` has four fixed sheets and `Q=Z`; no symbolic
+all-`D` SNF claim is made. The Bezout words are `alpha beta^-1` for `D=6k+1`
+and `alpha^2 beta^3` for `D=6k+5`; each SNF uses the actual relator
+`alpha^3 beta^(-4D)`, and mirrors use the generator swap.
+
+Route this immediately to different-model replay. Controls: original rep counts
+and H1 ranks before augmentation, multiple Schreier trees, simultaneous
+conjugacy, shifted Bezout pairs, mirror swap, and the exact `N=1` positive
+control `det([[p,-q],[e,f]])=pf+qe=1`, hence `Q=0`. A confirmed `Q!=0` kills
+only the enumerated representation; completeness of the case-(A) census is
