+   `E=F^{-1}(A_F)` smooth and `F|E:E->A_F\{c}=C*` étale;
+2. `chi(E)=1` forces some connected component to be `A^1`;
+3. a morphism `A^1->C*` is constant because the only units of `C[t]` are
+   constants, contradicting dominance.
+
+This claims case (A) empty for every `N>=2`, independently of the measured N8
+ledger `[CG:43-75]`. Its separate peripheral-rank/meridian-span chain kills the
+same profile again. Promote only after checking the no-cusp-preimage lemma,
+the `chi(E)=1` hypotheses, component dominance, and that both chains use the
+global case-(A) group rather than a forbidden local pushforward.
+
+The new proof attack is to extract exactly the case-(A) step that can cross to
+B3. Let `S=Sing(A_F)`. If one can prove
+
+```text
+OPEN[B3-SINGULAR-AVOID]:   F^{-1}(S)=empty,
+```
+
+then `E` is smooth and maps to `A_F^sm`. Again `chi(E)=1` supplies an `A^1`
+component. The normalization of a B3 curve loses the cusp preimage, at least
+two preimages of its multibranch point, and its point(s) at infinity; hence
+`A_F^sm` has at least two punctures. A nonconstant morphism from `A^1` to a
+rational curve with at least two punctures is impossible (move two punctures
+to `0,infinity` and use `C[t]^*=C*`). This would close B3 cofinally.
+
+The entire burden is the displayed singular-avoidance statement. It does not
+follow from a representation, from the case-(A) cusp lemma by analogy, or from
+the N4 topology. Test its proof on the exact `Gamma` B3 regression and require
+it to identify the first failed hypothesis; absent that proof, return typed
+`OPEN`, not a B3 kill.
