+## 4. New mechanism and cross-connection
+
+### `A2-SL2/DEV-RESULTANT` — a genuinely new mechanism
+
+On a simultaneous-top cell with `U>=3e+2`, the structural degrees and E0 give
+
+```text
+n = U-e,       sigma = (U+e)/2,
+deg q = U,     deg s = sigma,
+deg r' = n-1,  deg p' = 3n/2-1,
+2(q r' - p' s) = kappa != 0.
+```
+
+Here every prime means `partial_Z` by the source convention
+`[xmodel/cell-32-spec-sol56-20260901.md:43-45]`; longer formulas spell the
+derivative out to avoid ambiguity.
+
+Thus
+
+```text
+             [ q   p' ]
+M(Z) =       [ s   r' ]       has det M = kappa/2 in C*.
+```
+
+This is not an analogy: after a constant rescaling, `M` is an element of
+`SL_2(C[Z])`. On this `U>=3e+2` branch, the two degree differences are
+the same nonnegative integer
+
+```text
+t := deg(p')-deg(q) = deg(r')-deg(s) = (U-3e-2)/2.
+```
+
+Moreover
+
+```text
+r'/s - p'/q = kappa/(2qs).
+```
+
+The right side is strictly proper at infinity, so the polynomial parts of
+`p'/q` and `r'/s` coincide. Call that common quotient `H(Z)`, `deg H=t`, and
+write
+
+```text
+p' = Hq + ptilde,       r' = Hs + rtilde.
+```
+
+Then `q rtilde-ptilde s=kappa/2`; equivalently the elementary column operation
+`C_2 <- C_2-H C_1` preserves the unit determinant and strictly reduces the
+second column. Repeating the Euclidean algorithm gives a continued-
+fraction/elementary-matrix word for `M`. `E0` alone permits arbitrary word
+length; any Mason–Stothers bound must therefore consume other equations.
+
+Before choosing a complement, the directly rederived E0/O0/O1 give a sharper
+compatibility test. Put
+
+```text
+W = q partial_Z(s) - partial_Z(q) s,
+T = -(C1 partial_Z(E1)-partial_Z(C1) E1)/2
+    -3 D1 partial_Z(s)/4 + partial_Z(D1) s/4 - ZW/2.
+```
+
+Then E0, O0, and O1 are exactly the following three affine rows in the two
+source variables `(r',p')`:
+
+```text
+[q,  -s ] [r',p']^t = kappa/2,
+[C1,-E1] [r',p']^t = -W/2,
+[C2,-E2] [r',p']^t = T.
+```
+
+Their augmented determinant must vanish, giving the unreviewed exact identity
+
+```text
+D := (s C1-q E1)T + (W/2)(s C2-q E2)
+     + (kappa/2)(E1 C2-C1 E2) = 0.                 (DET-EO)
+```
+
+This uses only E0/O0/O1, which `[AU]` rederived directly `[AU:67-70]`; it does
+not consume SPEC's flawed E2. The tempting specialization to the old E1 wall
+and RAY-2 is illegal: the corrected E2 contains `-2qE1`, the wall is underived,
+and RAY-2 is refuted `[AU:805-816]`.
+
+The new move is to substitute `[AU]`'s free-`c` deviations
+
+```text
+X=4b eta^2 r-s^2,        Y=4b^2 eta q-3a s^2
+```
+
+into `DET-EO` and reduce it with the corrected, `s`-free EQ1–EQ3 system. Away
+from `c=-2e`, `[AU]` proves `deg X,deg Y<=4e-1`, independent of `U`
+`[AU:72-102]`. Thus compute a fixed-width elimination/resultant in
+`(eta,G,X,Y,c,kappa)` for each `e`, seeking a second relation in `(c,sigma)`.
+A nonzero resultant with `[AU]`'s `R(e,c,sigma,k)` would bound `sigma`; a
+factor only in `c` proposes a wall; zero exposes a dependency. Treat
+`c=-2e`, the other named exceptional `c` values, and the N-degenerate branch
+separately. A fixed `(e,c)` finite box is never reported as global A2 finiteness.
+
+Any reconstruction still branches on `A0=sC1-qE1=0`. On `A0!=0`, compute the
+reduced Bezout pair in `C[Z]`, require zero remainder in O0, reconstruct the
+derivatives `p',r'`, and check their declared source images. A nonzero constant
+kills only that branch; an identity is only a necessary-system signal.
+
+This cross-connects Avenue 29's corrected deviation identities with Avenue 5's
+elementary descent at an exact one-variable PID client. It also enforces
+the raw-degree guardrail: an elementary factorization of `M` is not yet a legal
+source or target automorphism of `F`. The lane must exhibit the map from the
+matrix column operation to the original normal-form variables before declaring
+`U` gauge.
+
+### Safe analytic/group bridge
+
+Do not identify the A2 cell and B3 curve by their shared “horn” label. First
+produce `OPEN[A2-TO-B3-OBJECT-MAP]`: from a full analytic solution, output the
+actual divisor or boundary valuation representing `A_F` and the pullback
