+## 11. Allocation, falsifiers, and close
+
+Allocate frontier effort in this order: (1) independent review and ledger merge
+of the A2 P0 and all-`N` case-(A) closure; (2) corrected WALL-PIN/DEV-RESULTANT
+and its exceptional branches; (3) one `Gamma` test of a singular-preimage B3 invariant;
+(4) a preflighted B2/B3/reducible `N=6` census, with prime seven only if it
+shrinks that queue; (5) joint companion/source-open completion.
+
+The portfolio changes direction on clear falsifiers. If independent source
+expansion does not reproduce `-2qE1`, quarantine `[AU]`; if it does, retire all
+old wall verdicts. If either case-(A) proof loses a source hypothesis, reopen
+only that chain. If the `c`-eliminant vanishes, study the dependency instead of
+calling `U` bounded. If a B3 invariant misses `Gamma`'s singular preimage or
+Euler ledger, archive it. If curve preflight fails, launch no solver.
+
+The central conclusion is deliberately negative about architecture: exact
