+## 4. New mechanism and cross-connection
+
+### `A2-SL2/DEV-RESULTANT` — a genuinely new mechanism
+
+On a simultaneous-top cell with `U>=3e+2`, the structural degrees and E0 give
+
+```text
+n = U-e,       sigma = (U+e)/2,
+deg q = U,     deg s = sigma,
+deg r' = n-1,  deg p' = 3n/2-1,
+2(q r' - p' s) = kappa != 0.
+```
+
+Here every prime means `partial_Z` by the source convention
+`[xmodel/cell-32-spec-sol56-20260901.md:120]`; longer formulas spell the
+derivative out to avoid ambiguity.
+
+Thus
+
+```text
+             [ q   p' ]
+M(Z) =       [ s   r' ]       has det M = kappa/2 in C*.
+```
+
+This is not an analogy: after a constant rescaling, `M` is an element of
+`SL_2(C[Z])`. On this `U>=3e+2` branch, the two degree differences are
+the same nonnegative integer
+
+```text
+t := deg(p')-deg(q) = deg(r')-deg(s) = (U-3e-2)/2.
+```
+
+Moreover
+
+```text
+r'/s - p'/q = kappa/(2qs).
+```
+
+The right side is strictly proper at infinity, so the polynomial parts of
+`p'/q` and `r'/s` coincide. Call that common quotient `H(Z)`, `deg H=t`, and
+write
+
+```text
+p' = Hq + ptilde,       r' = Hs + rtilde.
+```
+
+Then `q rtilde-ptilde s=kappa/2`; equivalently the elementary column operation
+`C_2 <- C_2-H C_1` preserves the unit determinant and strictly reduces the
+second column. Repeating the Euclidean algorithm gives a continued-
+fraction/elementary-matrix word for `M`. `E0` alone permits arbitrary word
+length; any Mason–Stothers bound must therefore consume other equations.
+
+Before choosing a complement, the directly rederived E0/O0/O1 give a sharper
+compatibility test. Put
+
+```text
+W = q partial_Z(s) - partial_Z(q) s,
+T = -(C1 partial_Z(E1)-partial_Z(C1) E1)/2
+    -3 D1 partial_Z(s)/4 + partial_Z(D1) s/4 - ZW/2.
+```
+
+Then E0, O0, and O1 are exactly the following three affine rows in the two
+source variables `(r',p')`:
+
+```text
+[q,  -s ] [r',p']^t = kappa/2,
+[C1,-E1] [r',p']^t = -W/2,
+[C2,-E2] [r',p']^t = T.
+```
+
+Their augmented determinant must vanish, giving the unreviewed exact identity
+
+```text
+D := (s C1-q E1)T + (W/2)(s C2-q E2)
+     + (kappa/2)(E1 C2-C1 E2) = 0.                 (DET-EO)
+```
+
+Here `E2` is the coefficient polynomial `E2(Z)=b Z eta^2`, not the equation
+called E2 in SPEC; call the latter `EQ2_even`. `DET-EO` uses only E0/O0/O1,
+which `[AU]` rederived directly `[AU:67-70]`, and does not consume flawed
+`EQ2_even`. The tempting specialization to the old E1 wall and RAY-2 is
+illegal: corrected `EQ2_even` contains `-2qE1`, the wall is underived,
+and RAY-2 is refuted `[AU:805-816]`.
+
+The decisive new move in corrected Chamber II is a **projection to the free
+`c`-line**. Substitute `[AU]`'s deviations
+
+```text
+X=4b eta^2 r-s^2,        Y=4b^2 eta q-3a s^2
+```
+
+into the corrected `s`-free EQ1–EQ3. Away from `c=-2e`, `[AU]` proves
+`deg X,deg Y<=4e-1`, independent of `U` `[AU:72-102]`. For fixed `e`, let
+`I_e` be their coefficient ideal in the explicitly ordered rational ring
+
+```text
+Q[eta_0..eta_(e-1), G_0..G_(2e-1), X_0..X_(4e-1),
+  Y_0..Y_(4e-1), kappa, tt, c],
+a=b=eta_e=1 (S1/S2), c5=0 (licensed C32 shear), G_(2e)=c,
+kappa*c*(c+2e)*tt-1=0,
+```
+
+using a block elimination order with every variable but `c` in the first
+block. Compute `J_e=I_e intersect Q[c]`. If `1 in I_e`, the declared main
+branch is empty. If `J_e` contains a nonconstant polynomial, `c` has finitely
+many candidates; in branch (A), for each fixed `k<=4e-1` with `k!=2e` and
+outside the named exceptional values, `[AU]`'s `R(e,c,sigma,k)` then leaves
+finitely many `sigma`. The entire vanished-factor stratum `k=2e`—including
+`deg X=deg Y=2e`, not covered by the named unequal-degree branch—is a separate
+`OPEN[A2-K2E]`. If `J_e=0`, the `s`-free subsystem does not pin `c`; feed its locus to
+the `s`-dependent EQ4/O1s instead. `DET-EO`, being a consequence of those same
+rows, is a checksum there, not an extra equation.
+
+Treat `c=0` as Chamber III; split `c=-2e`, `c=-(2e+1)`, Wall A
+`3c+6e+2=0`, `OPEN[A2-K2E]`, and Chamber I. Any SL2 reconstruction branches on
+`A0=sC1-qE1=0`; on `A0!=0`, compute the reduced Bezout pair over the solved
+coefficient field, branching on every Euclidean subresultant and leader;
+reconstruct `p',r'` and check O0 coefficientwise plus their source images. A fixed `(e,c)` finite box
+is never global A2 finiteness, and none of this supplies an actual map.
+
+This cross-connects Avenue 29's deviations with Avenue 5's elementary descent.
+Factoring `M` is not a legal source/target automorphism; that map remains
+`OPEN`, so it cannot make `U` gauge.
+
+### Safe analytic/group bridge
+
+Do not identify the A2 cell and B3 curve by their shared “horn” label. First
+produce `OPEN[A2-TO-B3-OBJECT-MAP]`: from a full analytic solution, output the
+actual divisor or boundary valuation representing `A_F` and the pullback
+`E=F^{-1}(A_F)`. Only then compare the signature
+
+```text
+(#components(E), genus(normalization(E)), #places_infinity(E),
+ local branch types, cover cycle types).
+```
+
+At `N=4`, B3 predicts this signature exactly in terms of the number and parity
+of double-point contacts `[HF:315-349]`, whereas the explicit A2 source chart
+under its rank-four hypothesis has geometric degree eight. Those are not
+comparable objects as currently written. If a future route lands in the same
+degree and profile, a mismatch kills that routed cell and a match merely
+licenses construction. Without the divisor-valued route, the bridge remains
+typed `OPEN`, not filled by the packet's “same object” wording.
+
+## 5. Strongest proof attack
+
+### Harvest and audit `CUSP-A-VOID`
+
+The strongest landed attack is `[CG]`'s `CUSP-A-VOID` (`PROVED-HERE /
+UNREVIEWED`). In case (A), its first chain is short enough to audit before any
+more census work:
+
+1. the cusp of `A_F` has no preimage, so local étaleness makes
+   `E=F^{-1}(A_F)` smooth and `F|E:E->A_F\{c}=C*` étale;
+2. `chi(E)=1` forces some connected component to be `A^1`;
+3. a morphism `A^1->C*` is constant because the only units of `C[t]` are
+   constants, contradicting dominance.
+
+This claims case (A) empty for every `N>=2`, independently of the measured N8
+ledger `[CG:43-75]`. Its separate peripheral-rank/meridian-span chain kills the
+same profile again. Promote only after checking the no-cusp-preimage lemma,
+the `chi(E)=1` hypotheses, component dominance, and that both chains use the
+global case-(A) group rather than a forbidden local pushforward. In Chain II
+use only the one-way fact that each component-basis meridian occurs among fixed
+lifts; do not biject components with fixed sheets, and allow repetitions.
+
+Do not transfer this proof to B3. The exact N4 regression forces a cusp preimage
+`y_0`, makes `E` singular there, and gives `chi_c(E)=1-4k`, not `1`
+`[HF:315-349]`. Thus both load-bearing steps fail before any units argument.
+This is a useful negative cross-connection: it scopes the all-degree case-(A)
+closure and says a B3 proof must consume its singular preimages rather than
+delete them. `Gamma` should reject any proposed invariant that silently imports
+smoothness or `chi(E)=1`; a safe replacement remains typed `OPEN`.
+
+## 6. Strongest counterexample / falsification attack
+
+Run `CORRECTED-DEVBOX-SHOOTER`. Rebuild all seven E/O equations from the source
+Even/Odd identities, including `-2qE1`; keep `c` free and impose no retired
+wall. In Chamber II branch (A), with `c!=-2e`, use
+`deg X,deg Y<=4e-1` to solve the fixed-width deviation box, then reconstruct
+`q,r`, the E0 Bezout data, and finally `p`. Search exceptional `c`, the full
+`OPEN[A2-K2E]` stratum, and Chambers I/III under their own bounds separately. This outranks
+an undifferentiated `S_6` search because a landed full solution has an explicit
+route toward a polynomial pair, whereas a permutation tuple does not.
+
+The state ladder is mandatory:
+
+```text
+SUBSYSTEM_POINT
+  -> FULL_EO_POINT in the declared quotient R
+  -> ADMISSIBLE_PULLBACK (all opens, boundary/general-fibre data,
+                          and [K:C(f,g)]=4 checked)
+  -> POLYNOMIAL_KELLER_PAIR under the explicit source chart
+  -> COUNTEREXAMPLE only after noninvertibility/geometric degree is certified.
+```
+
+The explicit chart
+`A=x^2, U=x+x^3y, Z=2y+x^2y^2` sends any landed full quotient solution to a
+polynomial pair with constant Jacobian. Conditional on the separately checked
+rank-four condition, its geometric degree is `2*4=8`; thus a terminating
+admissible solution would be counterexample-level rather than a representation
+(`xmodel/theta-reopen-explicit-pullback-sol56-20260831.md:412-449`). None of
+those later arrows may be inferred from a residual cell.
+
+Outcomes are deliberately symmetric. A unit ideal with positive and negative
+controls is a proof lead for that declared branch. Rank deficiency supplies
+only a candidate kernel: require augmented-rank compatibility at every level,
+all exceptional branches, and both terminal/bottom boundary conditions before
+calling it a recurrence. A terminating orbit is checked directly in `R`, then
+through the source chart. A formal or nonterminating orbit is only formal;
+vanished leaders and missing ring maps return typed `OPEN`.
+
+In parallel but second priority, build the `N=6` census around actual curves.
+The `N=4` B3 Keller realization is impossible; its representation/curve data
+are regression controls, not a counterexample target. Their value is to force
+any proposed group-to-geometry bridge to find the missing obstruction before
+that bridge is trusted at `N=6`.
+
+## 7. Software acceleration and decisive experiment
+
+### `CORRECTED-DEVBOX`
+
+Retire the old wall-cell generator: its `EQ2_even` omitted `-2qE1`, so its outputs are
+not free-`c` oracles `[AU:734-747]`. Build a source-first deviation
+engine instead:
+
+1. regenerate all seven coefficient identities from Even/Odd; emit the
+   coefficient field, ordered generators, and source-to-residual images, and
+   exact-diff every image;
+2. substitute `X,Y`, clear only declared powers of `eta`, and verify the
+   corrected `s`-free EQ1–EQ3 identities coefficientwise;
+3. in Chamber II, for each fixed integer `e` and `c!=-2e`, use the branch-(A)
+   caps `deg X,deg Y<=4e-1`; specialize `sigma` with its parity/domain
+   map rather than pretending varying-size systems form one `Q(e,U,j)` ring;
+4. run fraction-free linear algebra/resultants, branching on every pivot and
+   named exceptional `c`; generate separate Chamber-III and Chamber-I jobs
+   using their respective `4e-1` and `2g-1` caps; use two engines with explicit
+   Rabinowitsch variables, never a `sat()` wrapper;
+5. return `UNIT_IDEAL`, `COMPATIBLE_CANDIDATE_KERNEL`, or typed
+   `OPEN[branch/ring map]`, plus all specialization images.
+
+Smallest useful test: make old `EQ2_even` fail by exactly `-2qE1`; retain wall-imposed
+`(1,3)` EMPTY only as a stale-wall canary; require corrected free-`c` decisions
+for `(1,3),(1,5),(1,7)` from scratch; and preserve a synthetic
+shifted-generator positive control, labeled as synthetic rather than a
+full-system point. Rank loss is not a recurrence
+until augmented ranks, exceptional branches, and both boundary conditions pass.
+Stop the stale box01 extension and relaunch only corrected jobs.
+
+## 8. Detailed idea cards
+
+### Card 1 — `DEV-PROJECTION / WALL-PIN`
+
+**Dependencies:** reviewed A2 P0, corrected Chamber-II s-free EQ1–EQ3,
+branch-(A) deviation bounds, legal opens, and explicit `c` strata. **Cheapest discriminator:** compute
+`J_1=I_1 intersect Q[c]` in the declared DEVBOX ring. **Outcomes:** unit ideal
+kills that main branch; nonconstant `J_1` gives finitely many `c` candidates;
+`J_1=0` sends the returned locus to EQ4/O1s. None is an actual map. **Stop:**
+after the generic/exceptional split—no retired wall or monotone-cell work.
+**Information gain:** **extreme**, because wall pinning, true freedom, and
+emptiness separate in one calculation.
+
+### Card 2 — `GAMMA-B3-REGRESSION -> N6`
+
+The banked curve `Gamma:y^2=x^3(x-1)^2`, parametrized by
+`(t^2,t^3(t^2-1))`, has exactly a `(2,3)` cusp and one transverse node
+(`xmodel/block-descent-a1-quartic-cycle1-pseudoplane-companion-threat-map-sol56-20260830.md:355-387`): an exact curve-level B3 `k=1` control.
+**Dependencies:** complete projection census, native ZvK both orientations,
+all `S_4` tuples, and an invariant permitting the forced cusp preimage.
+**Cheapest discriminator:** make it reproduce `y_0`, `chi_c(E)=1-4k`, and the
+predicted genus/ends on `Gamma`. **Outcomes:** failure rejects the invariant;
+agreement licenses an `N=6` formulation but proves no emptiness; group data
+alone leave `OPEN`. **Stop:** one audited regression, then generalize or
+archive—no more degree-four curves.
+**Information gain:** **high mechanism value, no direct closure**.
+
+### Card 3 — `PRIME-7-SCOUT / PROFILE-FIRST-CENSUS`
+
+**Dependencies:** declared `N=7` B2/B3 profiles, faithful encodings, and explicit
+degree/transitivity/transposition checks. **Cheapest discriminator:** fix a
+meridian up to conjugacy and enumerate with Schreier–Sims. Prime transitivity
+gives primitivity; only an actual transposition pins `S_7`. **Outcomes:** zero
+is a profile screen absent coverage; survivors select at most two curve
+families and can simplify composite `N=6`; other cycle types retain their real
+subgroups. **Stop:** after representation classification, or immediately if
+the `N=6` queue is not reduced. **Information gain:** **medium-high at desk
+cost**, never an `N=6` substitute.
+
